# Line endings are normalized to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, git on Windows checks text files out with CRLF by default, and
# three things in this repository read text and compare it: `readlines` over the
# bundled `.dat` databases, the doctests, and `test/scripts.jl`, which checks
# that each generated script still matches the page it came from. That last one
# compares syntax trees rather than bytes and so survives either ending, but the
# other two are one stray `\r` away from a failure that says nothing about the
# code.
#
# LF everywhere also keeps a diff from showing every line of a file as changed
# the first time a Windows contributor saves it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, left exactly as they are.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
